{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","is_bot":false,"login":"konard","name":"Konstantin Diachenko"},"baseRefName":"main","body":"Fixes #924.\n\n## Summary\n\n- require every release cycle to include a merged, session-backed pull request authored end to end by Formal AI; every non-merge commit introduced by that PR must carry valid evidence for the same PR\n- ratchet the self-hosting target so the required share never decreases, record qualifying PR URLs in the release ledger, and retain the existing review, CI, promotion, metric, and evidence gates\n- execute compound self-development work through the Agent CLI whole-task-first, split failures into the smallest useful child tasks, verify the composed workspace, and keep learning proposals human-gated\n- preserve a verified child composition instead of unconditionally rerunning a destructive parent task, and apply the existing Python startup allowance consistently across platforms\n- document and check in replayable execution and pull-request contracts, a real incremental run, release case studies, and generated self-AST metadata\n\n## Root causes\n\nThe previous release metric could report success without a qualifying PR, and a PR with one attributed commit plus unrelated human commits could pass. Incremental execution also always retried the parent after successful children, which could overwrite a correct composition. Separately, the Python startup floor used by Agent CLI tests was Windows-only, leaving macOS workers with a brittle five-second budget under load.\n\n## Formal AI replay\n\n`experiments/issue_924_self_authoring/run.sh` ran the implementation task through Formal AI's Agent CLI. The whole task failed first, then decomposed into three independently verified children. The composed verifier accepted the resulting workspace without another mutating parent run.\n\n- trace: five steps (failed root, three passing Agent children, passing composed verifier)\n- native Agent sessions: four; the verifier is deliberately non-native and excluded from learning\n- authorship demonstration: two of the six smallest implementation leaves (33%)\n- replay sessions: `ses_ffc6f0044ffe6MkdE17jSHX1m4` and `ses_ffc6ef310ffeXG6Gb2BamMWTFb`\n- learning: proposal-only, four observations, human-gated, no proposal auto-applied\n- evidence: `docs/case-studies/issue-924/incremental-self-authorship/`\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\nRegression tests first reproduced:\n\n1. a mixed-authorship PR incorrectly satisfying the end-to-end release requirement\n2. a successful child composition being corrupted by the mandatory parent retry\n3. Python startup receiving only five seconds on non-Windows workers\n\nVerification completed locally:\n\n- `cargo fmt --check`\n- `cargo clippy --lib --bins --tests --all-features`\n- `cargo check --examples --all-features`\n- `rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs`\n- `rust-script scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs`\n- `cargo test --lib --bins --tests --all-features --verbose` (2,778 core tests passed, plus all integration binaries)\n- `cargo test --doc --verbose`\n- focused issue #924 release, evidence, replay, and incremental-composition suites\n- issue #991 Agent CLI dispatch/decomposition integration suite\n- generated-data regeneration (472 documents, zero rewrites on the final pass)\n- base-diff secret scan and `git diff --check`\n\n## Dependencies\n\nE69 supplies the merged write-effect foundation. E74 remains represented by #1004; this PR uses the already-supported direct Agent CLI execution path and does not weaken any existing review or promotion control.\n","closedAt":"2026-08-15T05:30:50Z","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABO-oTSg","author":{"login":"konard"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"\r\n\r\nWe need make the analysis deeper and fully implement vision from the issue using auto learning, and same task execution using Formal AI via Agent CLI, with incremental decomposition, so if big task is failing, we try to split them and solve them using Formal AI and Agent CLI locally, and continue splitting until tasks are fully solvable by Formal AI, if tasks fail, we must add just enough code for Formal AI to pass them all via generalization. Eventually Formal AI must learn to code itself, but in this pull request we must at least do a significant step towards this vision.\r\n\r\nSee our contributing guidelines, testing guidelines, vision, roadmap and so on. I expect this pull request to cover the most ambitious of requirements through generalization of logic, reasoning, advancing our meta algorithm to the highest possible potential. If you see something that still obsolete or contradicts generalization - it must be fixed.\r\n\r\nIt is ok to change architecture to move toward our goals of generalization in any place you touch.\r\n\r\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.","createdAt":"2026-08-15T02:48:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/1007#issuecomment-5300163402","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABO-o1jA","author":{"login":"konard"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"🤖 **AI Work Session Started**\n\nStarting automated work session at 2026-08-15T02:50:21.776Z\n\nThe PR has been converted to draft mode while work is in progress.\n\n_This comment marks the beginning of an AI work session. Please wait for the session to finish, and provide your feedback._","createdAt":"2026-08-15T02:50:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/1007#issuecomment-5300172172","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABO_K-2A","author":{"login":"konard"},"authorAssociation":"